---
title: What happens when the player types /aqr plan
---
sequenceDiagram
autonumber
actor Player
participant Slash as SlashCmdList
participant Chain as CommandHandler chain
participant Router as AtlasQuestRouter (Facade)
participant Api as IGameApi (Adapter)
participant Planner as QuestRoutePlanner
participant Builder as WorldGraphBuilder
participant Factory as AtlasSolverFactory
participant Atlas as AtlasSolver
participant UI as UserInteractions
Player->>Slash: /aqr plan
Slash->>Router: runCommand("plan")
Router->>Chain: handle("plan", "", router)
Chain->>Chain: Help? Add? ... no, pass on
Chain->>Router: PlanCommand.execute -> plan()
Router->>Api: currentLocationName(), playerProfile()
Router->>Planner: plan(profile, quests, start)
Planner->>Builder: reset().addLocations().addWalkingNetwork()...setStart()
Builder->>Builder: TravelLinkFactory.create + AccessRule chain per link
Builder-->>Planner: graph + required edges R
Planner->>Factory: create("quest")
Factory-->>Planner: AtlasSolver
loop while R has available edges (one game frame each)
  Planner->>Atlas: extend(): local DAG -> DP longest path -> best chain
  Atlas->>Atlas: append chain, mark served steps
end
Atlas-->>Planner: tour
Planner-->>Router: RoutePlan
Router->>UI: showPlan(plan) on chat + guide window
UI-->>Player: first step + arrow in the guide window
